|---|---|---|---|
| Customer ID (key) | string |  | Customer ID |
| Customer Name | string |  | Customer Name |
| Email | string |  | Email |
| Email Domain | string |  | Email Domain |
| Segment | string |  | Segment |
| City | string |  | City |
| State | string |  | State |
| Join Date | dateTime, format yyyy-mm-dd |  | Join Date |
| Loyalty Tier | string | Bronze, Silver, Gold; blanks become Unassigned. | Loyalty Tier |
| Account Managers | string | Parsed names joined with "; "; blank when the list is empty. | Account Managers |
| Account Manager Count | int64, format 0 |  | Account Manager Count |
| Lifetime Sales | double, format \\$#,0 | Context transition: every order of the customer, all statuses. | calculated (DAX) |
| Has Orders | string |  | calculated (DAX) |
| Value Tier | string |  | calculated (DAX) |

#### Measures

| Measure | Format | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Customer Count | `#,0` | Customers in the filter context (cross-filtered by Orders, both directions). |

##### Customer Count

Customers in the filter context (cross-filtered by Orders, both directions).

```dax
COUNTROWS(Customers)
```

#### Calculated columns

##### Lifetime Sales

Context transition: every order of the customer, all statuses.

```dax
CALCULATE(SUM(Orders[Line Amount]))
```

##### Has Orders

```dax
IF(ISEMPTY(RELATEDTABLE(Orders)), "No", "Yes")
```

##### Value Tier

```dax
SWITCH(
    TRUE(),
    Customers[Lifetime Sales] >= 3000, "High",
    Customers[Lifetime Sales] >= 1000, "Medium",
    Customers[Lifetime Sales] > 0, "Low",
    "None"
)
```

