## Shared expressions

### fnCleanKey

Power Query (M) expression, query group `Functions`.

Trims and upper-cases a business key (customer, store and product ids).

```powerquery
(x as text) as text => Text.Upper(Text.Trim(x))
```

### fnParseNames

Power Query (M) expression, query group `Functions`.

Turns a Python-style list of names, such as ['Ana Ruiz', "O'Neil Park"], into "Ana Ruiz; O'Neil Park".

```powerquery
(raw as text) as text =>
let
    Trimmed = Text.Trim(raw),
    Inner = if Text.Start(Trimmed, 1) = "[" then Text.Range(Trimmed, 1, Text.Length(Trimmed) - 2) else Trimmed,
    Names = List.Transform(Text.Split(Inner, ","), each Text.Trim(Text.Trim(_), {"'", """"})),
    NonEmpty = List.Select(Names, each _ <> ""),
    Result = if List.IsEmpty(NonEmpty) then "" else Text.Combine(NonEmpty, "; ")
in
    Result
```

## Roles

### Region West

Sees the West region only: its stores, their orders, returns and targets.

Model permission: read.

Row filter on `Stores`:

```dax
Stores[Region] = "West"
```

### Store Manager

Dynamic security: a manager sees the stores whose Manager Email is the signed-in user.

Model permission: read.

Row filter on `Stores`:

```dax
Stores[Manager Email] = USERPRINCIPALNAME()
```
